---
// The ten features of "How the board works" in English, in the order you use
// the board. Layout and styles are in src/pages/[lang]/how-it-works.astro and
// src/components/HowFeature.astro; the boards and screenshots in
// src/data/howItWorks.ts.
import Feature from "../../../components/HowFeature.astro";
---

<Feature title="Starting lineups" image="lineup" alt="The board with the lineup vs 6-0.">
  On a new board, set out a lineup in one tap: against 6-0, 5-1 or 3-2-1, or two or three lines for a drill.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Drawing arrows" image="arrows" alt="A run by the left back and a pass to where it ends.">
  The board opens with Arrow on: drag from a player for a run, and from the ball for a pass.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Shooting" image="shot" alt="A shot at goal by the right back.">
  A pass that ends between the posts is a shot.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Kinds of arrow" image="kinds" alt="The six kinds of arrow side by side: run, pass, bounce, dribble, shot and screen.">
  Tap an arrow and pick run, pass, bounce, dribble, shot or screen.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Numbers and positions" image="labels" alt="Players with 7, 11 and LW.">
  Tap a player, then Number or position: type a jersey number, a position or initials, up to 3 characters.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Steps" image="steps">
  Tap New step for the next step and type one sentence per step: who does what.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Play" image="play" alt="The step bar with two steps, New step and the Play button.">
  Tap the button next to New step: the players move along their arrows, step by step.
</Feature>
<Feature title="Sharing" image="viewer" alt="A shared board in the viewer on a phone.">
  Everything is in the link or in the QR code in More, so your players see every step with its sentence, without an account or app.
</Feature>
<Feature title="My boards" image="my-boards" alt="My boards with the folders Tuesday and Thursday.">
  More holds your boards, saved in this browser, in folders in the order of your practice.
</Feature>
<Feature title="On another device" image="open-link" alt="Open a link with a pasted message of Share folder.">
  Paste the message of Share folder, or a single link, under Open a link in My boards: your boards are then on that device too.
</Feature>
